    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19660" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">glŏbōsus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		globus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>round as a ball</i>, <i>spherical</i>, <i>globose</i> (class.): (mundum)
			globosum est fabricatus, quod <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφαιροειδὲς</span> Graeci vocant, <i><span class="en">Cic.
				Univ. 6</span></i>; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stellae globosae et rotundae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Rep. 6, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mundus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					N. D. 2, 45, 116</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">forma (mundi),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 19, 49</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 39, 98</span></i>
			: saxum, Pac. ap. <i><span class="en">Auct. Her. 2, 23,
			36</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 38, 29, 4</span></i>.</div>
